  "grammar": {
    "topic": "Third and Fourth Conjugation Verbs",
    "explanation": "Third conjugation verbs have -ere (short e) infinitives and show an -i- theme vowel in most forms. Fourth conjugation verbs have -ire infinitives. Third conjugation -io verbs (like capio) conjugate like fourth conjugation in the present.",
